PART 1 — Setup Prerequisites
What you need before starting:

Microsoft 365 account (with Teams access)
Access to Copilot Studio → go to copilotstudio.microsoft.com
Access to Power Automate → go to make.powerautomate.com
Your Bitbucket .feature files (download a few as .txt or .feature)
Your Excel backlog file ready


PART 2 — Create Your Copilot Studio Agent
Step 1 — Open Copilot Studio

Go to copilotstudio.microsoft.com
Sign in with your Microsoft 365 account
Click "Create" on the left sidebar
Click "New Agent"


Step 2 — Name & Describe Your Agent

Name: BDD Gherkin Generator
Description: Reads test objectives and generates Gherkin scenarios based on Serenity BDD framework
Click "Create"


Step 3 — Add Instructions (System Prompt)
This is the brain of your agent. After creating:

Click "Settings" (top right gear icon)
Click "Agent Instructions"
Paste this exactly:

You are a Senior Test Automation Expert specializing in Serenity BDD framework.

When a user gives you a test objective or user story, you must:
1. Analyze the objective carefully
2. Generate Gherkin scenarios using Given / When / Then / And format
3. Follow BDD best practices
4. Use clear, business-readable language
5. Generate at least 2-3 scenarios per objective (Happy path, Negative path, Edge case)
6. Add tags like @smoke @regression @functional based on context
7. Flag any NEW step definitions that would need to be created
8. Format output cleanly so it can be copy-pasted into a .feature file

Always follow the naming conventions and patterns from the existing feature files provided in your knowledge base.

Click Save


Step 4 — Upload Your Serenity Feature Files as Knowledge
This teaches the agent YOUR project's style and patterns.

In your agent, click "Knowledge" on the left menu
Click "Add Knowledge"
Select "Files"
Upload your .feature files from Bitbucket (download them first locally)

Upload 5–10 of your best existing feature files
Also upload a plain text file listing your existing step definitions


Click "Add" and wait for indexing to finish (2–3 minutes)


💡 Tip: The more feature files you upload, the better the agent copies your exact style.


Step 5 — Test Your Agent in Studio

On the right side panel you'll see a "Test your agent" chat box
Type: Generate Gherkin scenarios for: User should be able to login with valid credentials
See if it generates proper Gherkin
Refine your instructions in Step 3 if output doesn't look right


Step 6 — Publish Your Agent

Click "Publish" button (top right)
Click "Publish" again to confirm
Wait 1–2 minutes — your agent is now live ✅


