The Fix — Use ONE Fixed File Location
Instead of triggering on "new file uploaded", we change the approach to:
Golden Rule:

Always read from one fixed Excel file in OneDrive. When you have updates, just replace/overwrite that same file. The flow reads whatever is currently there.


Revised Power Automate Flow Design
Step 1 — Change the Trigger
Remove the "When a file is created" trigger.
Replace with: Manually trigger a flow OR When a message is posted in Teams (so you or your team can trigger it on demand)
Best option for you → Teams trigger:

Search trigger: "When a keyword is mentioned" → Teams
Or simpler: Use "Manually trigger a flow" with a button


Step 2 — Always Read from Fixed File Path
In the "List rows present in a table" Excel step:

File: Hardcode the path to your ONE fixed Excel file

Example: /BDD Backlog/MyBacklog.xlsx


This means — every time flow runs, it reads whatever rows exist in that file at that moment


Step 3 — Track Already Processed Rows (So it doesn't re-generate old scenarios)
This is the smart part. You don't want it re-generating Gherkin for rows it already processed.
Add a "Status" column in your Excel:
Test IDTest ObjectiveModulePriorityStatusTC001Login with valid credentialsLoginHighDone ✅TC002Invalid password errorLoginMedium
In Power Automate — add a Condition inside the loop:

Inside "Apply to each" loop, add "Condition" action
Set condition: Status is not equal to Done
If Yes (empty status): → Call agent → Post to Teams → Update Excel row Status to "Done"
If No (already Done): → Do nothing (skip)

This way:

New rows (blank Status) → get processed ✅
Old rows (Status = Done) → skipped ✅


Step 4 — Update Row After Processing
After posting to Teams, add:

Search action: "Update a row" → Excel Online (Business)
Point to same file and table
Set Key Column: Test ID
Set Key Value: Current row's Test ID
Set Status column → type Done


Updated Daily Usage
When you have NEW backlog items:
  → Open your fixed Excel (MyBacklog.xlsx) in OneDrive
  → Add new rows (leave Status column BLANK)
  → Save file
  → Trigger the flow manually or via Teams

When you have NO changes:
  → Do nothing — old rows are already marked Done
  → Flow will skip them automatically

When you want to RE-GENERATE a scenario:
  → Clear the "Status" cell for that row
  → Trigger flow again

